+
+## E6 — the two shape files the audit said did not exist
+
+`tests/regression/loop_preheader_shapes.c` and
+`tests/regression/check_loop_preheader.sh` are the end-to-end coverage named
+by `src/passes/loop_preheader.rs`'s own docstring. Neither existed in the PR.
+
+**This file's first draft put the shapes in a subdirectory**, which dodged
+BLOCKER-1 rather than solving it: `run_regression.py` globs
+`tests/regression/*.c` non-recursively and builds each standalone, so a file
+that only makes sense next to another one would be compiled without its
+partner and fail with an undefined reference. Avoiding the glob hid the
+shapes from the corpus entirely.
+
+Upstream (`ms178/lccc#688`) later landed the same gate and solved it the
+better way: the fixture sits in the corpus root **and carries its own
+`main()`**, so the very shape it is written to pin is now also compiled and
+run by the corpus gate on every CI run. Hiding the fixture from the corpus
+would have made the "must stay byte-identical" contract unenforceable
+upstream of this gate; giving it a `main()` makes the corpus a second,
+independent witness to the same property. The subdirectory workaround was
+therefore dropped in favour of upstream's placement.
